{
 "description": {
  "what": "Paired comparison of two CityCompass land-use runs of Buenos Aires, 2022-2031, same seed (123456), same CLI bundle and flags: the baseline, and the same run with the new line (line.json: metro, opens 2023) plus its transit-oriented upzone (zoning-scenario.json: 38 m within 500 m of the 13 stations, from 2023).",
  "areas": "within = parcels whose centroid (../ba/parcels_centroid.f32) is within 800 m of a new station; elsewhere = every other parcel; upzonedParcels = the 10,668 parcels the zoning scenario raises to 38 m (all inside the 800 m rings). A building or demolition is placed by its first parcel (all run-built buildings stand on seed parcels).",
  "flows": "started = buildings whose construction started that year (the pre-run pipeline counts in 2022, as the exporter does); completed = completion date inside that year; demolitions = removal date inside that year. total = 2022-2031; from2023 = 2023-2031 (the years the line and upzone exist).",
  "population": "populationAtEnd/householdsAtEnd/unassignedHouseholdsAtEnd = the engine's December record (exports' totals). housedPersonsAtYearEnd/housedHouseholdsAtYearEnd = persons and households living on a parcel at each year end, from the run report's population replay of run.ccsr (households with no dwelling are in no area, so within + elsewhere = housed population, not total population).",
  "pairingCheck": "2022 is before the line and the upzone exist, so a correct pairing (same seed, same inputs) gives identical 2022 values.",
  "placebo": "Rings of 800 m around standing Subte stations at least 1600 m from every new station (and 1600 m from each other): places the scenario does not touch, so their change between the runs is what the two runs drift apart by chance plus any city-wide knock-on effect. Compare with the line's own rings."
 },
 "verdict": {
  "pairing": "2022 (before the line and the upzone exist) is identical in both runs, building ids included: the pairing holds, so every later difference comes from the scenario and what it set off.",
  "cityWide": "Small. 2023-2031, city-wide: buildings started 22,702 vs 22,697 (0%), units started 114,970 vs 118,671 (+3.2%), buildings completed 21,804 vs 21,749 (-0.3%), units completed 114,895 vs 117,462 (+2.2%), demolished buildings 12,570 vs 12,592 (+0.2%). Population at the end of 2031: 2,964,445 vs 2,964,445; households without a dwelling 16,876 vs 15,867.",
  "nearTheLine": "Large. Within 800 m of the 13 stations, 2023-2031: units started 5,757 vs 8,991 (+56.2%), buildings started 308 vs 381 (+23.7%), units completed 5,986 vs 8,465 (+41.4%), demolished buildings 327 vs 480 (+46.8%); median storeys of the ar-multifamily buildings started there 7 vs 12.",
  "noise": "Not noise near the line. The 16 placebo rings (standing Subte stations away from the line) move +1.6% in units started in total, a single ring by up to 49.9% (median 18.1%). The line's rings move +56.2% in total, and 7 of 13 rise by more than any placebo ring (Av. General Iriarte, Av. Caseros, Pavón, Hipólito Yrigoyen, Callao y Las Heras, Av. Pueyrredón, Plaza Italia). Rings that fell (Av. Corrientes -25.7%, Av. Córdoba -23.6%, Sánchez de Bustamante -2.1%, Jerónimo Salguero -40.4%) stay inside the placebo range. The line's rings are smaller (443 units started per ring in the baseline, against 1,530 per placebo ring), so their percentages swing more by chance: a single ring's change of a few tens of percent is chance, the corridor total (+3,234 units) is not; the largest placebo ring moves by 658 units.",
  "whereTheGainIs": "On the upzoned parcels: units started 1,588 vs 5,136 (+223.4%). The other parcels within 800 m: 4,169 vs 3,855 (-7.5%), inside the chance range. Elsewhere in the city: units started 109,213 vs 109,680 (+0.4%), buildings started 22,394 vs 22,316 (-0.3%).",
  "population": "Small. Persons living within 800 m at the end of 2031: 417,732 vs 420,671 (+0.7%); elsewhere 2,422,054 vs 2,421,439 (0%)."
 },
